    1 0000:              ;
    2 0000:              ; HBIOS for VIDEO-G 1.0 (System-5) on HBIOS v1.0.8: the ROM for the new card set (CPU Rev D, the IO panel, VIDEO-G).
    3 0000:              ; Made 2026-11-01 from HBIOS v1.0.4 for the VIDEO-G TEXT board; brought up to v1.0.8 on 2026-11-20 (Ken).
    4 0000:              ;
    5 0000:              ; For VIDEO-G (hardware/video-g/DESIGN.md sections 2, 3 and 8), in place of v1.0.4's 6845-card driver:
    6 0000:              ;   - VIDEO-G is memory-mapped (2026-11-17, hardware/video-g/DESIGN.md section 3): the 6845 at 7800 (address
    7 0000:              ;     register) and 7801 (data), as on the 6845 card; the key at 7802; status / control at 7804 (KEY-READY = bit 0)
    8 0000:              ;   - the 64 x 25 NTSC table (R0-R9 = 94,64,76,8,31,6,25,28,0,7; 8 x 8 cells), cursor rows 0-7
    9 0000:              ;   - the bottom row is row 24 (7600); the cursor is kept in 77FE/77FF as before (not displayed at 25 rows)
   10 0000:              ;   - the control register (7804) = 00 at start: text on, graphics, XOR and mouse off, page 0
   11 0000:              ;   - inchar and brk poll KEY-READY in the status register instead of EF3 (any CPU card: CPU Rev D takes the bus
   12 0000:              ;     -EF on EF4), read the key at 7802 and keep every register but D
   13 0000:              ;   - a line feed scrolls only the 24 visible rows (1536 bytes, twelve to a pass of the loop) and blanks row 24:
   14 0000:              ;     about 50 ms at 1.76 MHz, against 168 ms for the v1.0.4 copy of all of 7040-77FF
   15 0000:              ;   - the cursor address sent to R14/R15 is the 6845 address (RC - 7000), not the high byte of RC AND 3F
   16 0000:              ;   - a key of 80h or more (the VIDEO-G keyboard: F1-F12 80-8B, Home Up PgUp Left 5 Right End Down PgDn Ins Del
   17 0000:              ;     90-9A, with Shift C0-DA) is returned by inchar but not echoed (outchar strips bit 7: it would print junk)
   18 0000:              ;
   19 0000:              ; From v1.0.5 to v1.0.8, as in firmware/hbios/v1.0.8/sec1.asm (2026-11-20):
   20 0000:              ;   - the monitor's added commands: H (the list), B (boot the OS), D start:end (disassemble), Q1 / Q0, and the IO
   21 0000:              ;     panel demo at @F1C0. The disassembler's key wait reads VIDEO-G's keyboard (rawkey), where v1.0.8 has EF3 / INP 1
   22 0000:              ;   - the IO panel's real-time clock behind f_gettod and f_settod: the same bytes at the same addresses as v1.0.8
   23 0000:              ;     (FC92-FCEB and F7CD-F7FF)
   24 0000:              ;   - not here: v1.0.7's key codes at @F1E0 (written for the 6845 card and the old keyboard port). @F1E0 restarts
   25 0000:              ;     HBIOS in this ROM, so that the habit does no harm
   26 0000:              ; To make room in the 4K EPROM the line feed's copy is a loop of twelve bytes a pass (it was 64, 226 bytes of code at
   27 0000:              ; F300), and the pieces sit in the free runs: brk after the driver (F0D7), the rest of the H list and rawkey after
   28 0000:              ; inchar, Q1 / Q0 at F1E3, the scroll at FC45 after the disk fix. build.py checks that no piece runs into the next.
   29 0000:              ; build.py also gives it v1.0.6's disk fix (LBA mode, FBC1 / FBDF / FC31-FC44), which Elf/OS v5 needs, v1.0.5's
   30 0000:              ; hook into Mike Riley's monitor (F941, F9EB-F9ED) and v1.0.8's clock vectors (F816-F81A, FEDC).
   31 0000:              ; The jump table at F200 and the Riley code are as in v1.0.4.
   32 0000:              ;
   33 0000:              ;
   34 0000:              ; Define BIOS to generate code for use with ELFOS BIOS
   35 0000:              ;
   36 0000:              
   37 0000:              
   38 0000:              
   39 0000:              ;
   40 0000:              ; Define 6845VIDEOLOWER when video card (REV B and beyond) supports lower
   41 0000:              ; case characters and there is no need to force characters to upper case
   42 0000:              ;
   43 0000:              
   44 0000:              
   45 0000:              
   46 0000:              ;
